:: StoryTitle
Saltmarrow

:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "<generated by Twine>",
  "format": "Inkjot",
  "format-version": "0.6.0",
  "start": "prologue"
}

:: Inklink [config]
(((
Ex 9: a Zork-like `game`, solo, in general words only. A draft for Inkjot
v0.6, and `define`'s next test (docs/define.md): a spellbook of nineteen
spells, each with a cost, a range, and a power or a duration.

**The game.** Saltmarrow is an old salt mine under a fen town. Its salt
holds spells: a working is paid for with a crystal on the tongue. Your
master, Agnes Thwaite, went down three days ago and has not come up. You
go after her with her oil lamp, her primer, and four crystals of salt.

**The rules that make it this game:**

- **Salt is the only cost.** Spells cost crystals (`default cost: salt`);
  walking, taking and talking are free. Salt can be prised from the walls
  with a pick (which can break), found, bought, and scraped from the brine
  pans, which crust over again every few turns, so salt never runs out for
  good.
- **Fire.** A flame near dry timber starts a fire: the lamp, a spell, the
  Gleaner's candle, or firedamp in the north drift. Four of the fifteen
  places are timbered. A fire smoulders, burns, blazes, spreads to the
  nearest timbered place it touches, then burns out.
- **Burnt shafts.** The ladderway and the cribbed winze are timber. Burnt,
  each can be crossed three more times, with a warning each time (the mice
  leave, one by one), then falls in behind you.
- **No dead ends.** Every way that can fall has another beside it, by
  magic or by engineering: the cage (mended, or ridden on an updraught)
  for the ladderway, the flooded stair (drained, or drawn down) for the
  winze, the old adit (dug, or cleared) for the Warden's hall. The cage
  rope always goes *down*. Salt regrows at the pans and in the Marrow, and
  the pick is never the only way through. `tests/ex9_map.rs` plays it at
  random to check.
- **The Brinewarden** guards the way *out* of the deep: down is free, up is
  paid. Leave the shard of marrow salt behind and it lets you go. Take it,
  and it can be fought (fresh water unmakes salt), sneaked past (it feels
  warmth and hears footsteps), bargained with (it was never paid), or
  outrun (it walks only on salt, and slowly).

**`where:`** chooses for the rules: where a fire goes next, what the
Gleaner steals and where they wander, where the Warden steps as it
follows you, what Dowse points at.

What it asks of v0.6 beyond the plan is in the drafts README.
)))
kind: game
tags: fantasy ~ text adventure ~ puzzle ~ mine ~ spellbook
ages: 10..
mode: solo
pov: apprentice
narration: second person
clock: 0.. ~ shown as "turn"
start: prologue
default moves: walk
default takes: take, drop
default cost: salt

resource salt: 4 ~ max 12 ~ shown as "salt" ~ counted as "crystal"
resource hp: 3 ~ shown as "wounds left"
resource rewinds: 3 ~ shown as "undos"

rewind: undo
~ to any visited turn
~ keeps knows

on death
~ then play crushed

state score: 0 ~ track ~ shown as "score"

(((
The mine, top to bottom. Depth is in feet: `{plural(here.depth, "foot")}`
reads "120 feet" by the built-in irregulars.
)))
map mine: 5 by 4 ~ shows visited
~ pithead   | .            | .        | fen
~ ladderway | .            | .        | .
~ stables   | gallery      | chapel   | timber_yard
~ drift     | incline      | cribbing | brine_pans
~ marrow    | wardens_hall | sump     | adit

state depth: 0 ~ belongs to place
state heat: 0 ~ belongs to place
state burnt: no ~ belongs to place
state veins: 0 ~ belongs to place
state crust: 0 ~ belongs to place

archetype shaft ~ timbered
~ state crossings: 3
~ state fallen: no

place pithead: "the pithead" ~ way_out
place fen: "the fen" ~ way_out
place ladderway: "the ladderway" ~ like shaft ~ salted ~ with depth: 60
place stables: "the pony stables" ~ timbered ~ salted ~ with depth: 120
place gallery: "the Long Gallery" ~ salted ~ with depth: 120 ~ with veins: 3
place chapel: "the Salters’ Chapel" ~ salted ~ with depth: 120
place timber_yard: "the timber yard" ~ timbered ~ salted ~ with depth: 120
place incline: "the Incline" ~ timbered ~ salted ~ with depth: 240
place drift: "the north drift" ~ salted ~ with depth: 240
place brine_pans: "the brine pans" ~ salted ~ crusts ~ with depth: 240
place cribbing: "the cribbed winze" ~ like shaft ~ salted ~ with depth: 300
place wardens_hall: "the Warden’s hall" ~ salted ~ with depth: 360
place sump: "the sump" ~ salted ~ with depth: 380
place marrow: "the Marrow" ~ salted ~ crusts ~ with depth: 400
place adit: "the old adit" ~ salted ~ with depth: 380

state cage_fixed: no
state stair_water: 4
state rubble: 3
state propped: no
state planks_out: no
state air_door_open: no
state gas: 3
state flame_warned: no
state sluice_open: no

way ladder_top: pithead - ladderway ~ down ~ open when not ladderway.fallen
way ladder_foot: ladderway - gallery ~ down ~ open when not ladderway.fallen
way cage: pithead - incline ~ down ~ open when cage_fixed ~ shown as "the cage"
way cage_rope: pithead - incline ~ one way ~ down ~ shown as "down the cage rope"
way chapel_arch: gallery - chapel
way stalls: gallery - stables
way yard_gate: gallery - timber_yard
way back_stalls: stables - timber_yard ~ shown as "through the stalls"
way incline_head: gallery - incline ~ down
way pans_road: incline - brine_pans
way drift_mouth: incline - drift
way crib_top: drift - cribbing ~ open when not cribbing.fallen
way crib_foot: cribbing - wardens_hall ~ down ~ open when not cribbing.fallen
way flooded_stair: brine_pans - sump ~ down ~ open when stair_water == 0
way sump_door: sump - wardens_hall
way marrow_mouth: wardens_hall - marrow
way the_fall: marrow - adit ~ open when rubble == 0 ~ shown as "the fall"
way stop_planks: adit - fen ~ up ~ open when planks_out

(((
Fire. Each turn, in order: a blaze burns out and leaves the place burnt;
a smoulder or a fire grows; each blaze reaches the nearest timbered place
next to it that has not burnt and is not burning.
)))
on turn ends
~ then play fire:turn

on enter place when entered.heat >= 2
~ then play burned

on enter shaft when entered.burnt
~ then lower entered.crossings 1
~ then play shaft:creaks

on leave shaft when left.burnt and left.crossings == 0
~ then set left.fallen: yes
~ then play shaft:falls

on leave marrow when me.holds.shard
~ then play warden:wakes

on move warden when warden.roused and warden.here and not warden.unmade
~ then play warden:fight

on enter place when gleaner.here
~ then play gleaner:about

on enter place when thwaite.here and thwaite.with_me and not way_free
~ then play thwaite:waiting

fuse lamp_oil: 90 ~ shown as "lamp oil" ~ lit
~ then set lamp.lit: no
~ then set safety_lamp.lit: no

get open_flame: (me.holds.lamp and lamp.lit) or (gleaner.here and gleaner.candle_lit)
get seeing: (me.holds.lamp and lamp.lit) or (me.holds.safety_lamp and safety_lamp.lit) or me.glimmering or here.heat > 0
get way_free: thwaite.lightened or me.holds.stretcher or warden.paid
get burning_near: all(place, where: it.heat > 0 and it.next_to(here))

act take
act drop

archetype tool ~ state broken: no
archetype treasure ~ state counted: no

item lamp: "Thwaite’s oil lamp" ~ held by apprentice ~ catches
~ state lit: yes
item safety_lamp: "a gauzed safety lamp" ~ catches
~ state lit: yes
item gauze: "a cylinder of fine iron gauze" ~ in drift ~ hidden until drift.searched
item pick: "a short salt pick" ~ like tool ~ in timber_yard ~ breaks 1 in 6
item hammer: "a lump hammer" ~ like tool ~ in timber_yard
item hay: "fifty-year-dry hay" ~ in stables ~ fixed ~ catches ~ burns
~ state lit: no
item stop_planks: "the stop-planks" ~ in adit ~ fixed ~ catches
~ state lit: no
item spanner: "a long spanner" ~ like tool ~ in timber_yard
item stave: "a pit prop" ~ plural "staves" ~ in timber_yard ~ count 4 ~ burns
item sacking: "an old salt sack" ~ in timber_yard ~ burns
item stretcher: "a stretcher of two staves and a sack" ~ burns
item horseshoe: "a pony’s horseshoe" ~ in stables
item pawl: "an iron pawl, hammered from a horseshoe"
item oil_can: "a can of lamp oil" ~ in stables ~ fixed
item flask: "a stoppered flask" ~ held by apprentice
~ state water: empty
item tally: "a brass pay tally, stamped 41" ~ in stables ~ hidden until stables.searched
item salt_rose: "a rose carved from pink salt" ~ like treasure ~ in chapel
item brasses: "a strap of pony brasses" ~ like treasure ~ in stables
item shard: "a shard of marrow salt, clear as water" ~ like treasure ~ in marrow
item chest: "the salt chest" ~ in pithead ~ fixed

recipe stretcher: stave, stave, sacking ~ make ~ "Two staves and a sack, for carrying someone who cannot walk."
recipe pawl: horseshoe ~ using hammer ~ make ~ "A horseshoe, straightened and bent again into a catch."
recipe safety_lamp: lamp, gauze ~ make ~ "The gauze round the flame: it lets air in, and no fire out."

fact primer: "Thwaite’s primer: kindle, glimmer, quench, gust. *Salt on the tongue, then the word. Never the word first.*"
fact carving_hush: "Carved in the chapel: a working to walk unheard."
fact carving_ward: "Carved in the chapel: a working to turn one blow."
fact carving_tongue: "Carved in the chapel: a working to speak with what was made, not born."
fact notes_mending: "Thwaite’s notes: knit, for small breaks; shore, for timber that has burnt."
fact notes_weight: "Thwaite’s notes: lighten, so a thing weighs nothing for a while."
fact notes_greater: "Thwaite’s notes: two workings said as one make a greater. *Draw and sweeten. Kindle and gust. Glimmer and hush. Knit and shore. Gust and lighten.*"
fact boilers_charm: "Scratched on a brine pan: draw, to call water out of rock; sweeten, to take the salt out of it."
fact chalk_charm: "Chalked on the yard board: clear, to shift a fall of stone a load at a time."
fact dowsing: "Thwaite’s last working: dowse, to taste which way the air goes out."
fact never_paid: "Thwaite: *The Warden was made to guard the deep for a wage, and nobody ever paid it.*" ~ clue
fact blue_cap: "A lamp flame that stands up tall and blue means firedamp. Get the flame out, or yourself." ~ clue
fact warden_feels: "The Warden feels warmth and hears footsteps. It does not see." ~ clue

character apprentice: "Thwaite’s apprentice" ~ selectable ~ pronouns chosen ~ hp 3

npc thwaite: "Agnes Thwaite" ~ pronouns she ~ in marrow ~ moves none
~ follows me when self.with_me and way_free
npc warden: "the Brinewarden" ~ pronouns it ~ in wardens_hall
~ moves toward me 1 every 2 turns when self.roused and not self.paid and not self.unmade ~ where: it.salted and it.heat == 0
npc gleaner: "the Gleaner" ~ pronouns they ~ in stables
~ moves 1 per turn ~ where: it.salted and it.depth < 300 and it.heat == 0 and not it.like(shaft) and not (it == drift and gas > 0)

objective find: "Find Agnes Thwaite" ~ done when thwaite.found
objective bring: "Bring her up" ~ after find ~ done when thwaite.here and here.way_out

(((
Zork's ranks, in salt. A table read as a value.
)))
table rank: score
~ 0..=19: "a lamp carrier"
~ 20..=49: "a crust scraper"
~ 50..=79: "a pan-boiler"
~ 80..=99: "a deputy"
~ 100: "a saltwright"

:: apprentice [character]
state hushed: no
state glimmering: no
state shrouded: no
state tongued: no
state held: no
--
(((
The spellbook, in general words. Each spell is an act with `~ spell`, a
cost in salt, a description the platform shows in the book, and its
effect. Range is the `~ at` filter: touch is a thing here, *next* is a
place next to here, *self* has none. Power is a number in the effect;
duration is `~ for N turns`. So each spell says its numbers twice, once
for the reader and once for the engine. See the drafts README for what
`define` would change.
)))
act kindle: cost 1 ~ spell ~ fire ~ learned from primer
~ "A flame at your fingertip, for a wick or dry wood. Range: touch."
~ at item here where: it.catches and not it.lit
~ then set target.lit: yes
act glimmer: cost 1 ~ spell ~ light ~ learned from primer
~ "A cold light about you, with no heat in it. Self. Lasts 8 turns."
~ then set me.glimmering: yes ~ for 8 turns
act quench: cost 2 ~ spell ~ water ~ learned from primer
~ "Puts fire down: a blaze to a smoulder, a smoulder to nothing. Here. Power 2."
~ when here.heat > 0
~ then lower here.heat 2
act gust: cost 1 ~ spell ~ air ~ learned from primer
~ "One breath of wind, sent into the next place. Clears bad air; snuffs candles; feeds fires. Range: next."
~ at place where: it.next_to(here)
~ then set gas: 0 when target == drift
~ then set gleaner.candle_lit: no when gleaner.in(target)
~ then raise target.heat 1 when target.heat > 0
act hush: cost 2 ~ spell ~ quiet ~ learned from carving_hush
~ "Your steps make no sound. Self. Lasts 4 turns."
~ then set me.hushed: yes ~ for 4 turns
act ward: cost 2 ~ spell ~ learned from carving_ward
~ "A skin of salt that takes one blow. Self. Lasts 3 turns."
~ then cover me ~ for 3 turns
act tongue: cost 2 ~ spell ~ learned from carving_tongue
~ "Speech with things that were made, not born. Self. Lasts 6 turns."
~ then set me.tongued: yes ~ for 6 turns
act knit: cost 2 ~ spell ~ learned from notes_mending
~ "Mends a small break. Range: touch."
~ at item here where: it.broken
~ then set target.broken: no
act shore: cost 3 ~ spell ~ learned from notes_mending
~ "Timber that has burnt holds a while longer. Range: touch. Power 3: three more crossings."
~ when here.like(shaft) and here.burnt
~ then raise here.crossings 3
act lighten: cost 3 ~ spell ~ air ~ learned from notes_weight
~ "One thing, or one person, weighs nothing. Range: touch. Lasts 6 turns."
~ at person here where: it != me
~ then set target.lightened: yes ~ for 6 turns
act draw: cost 2 ~ spell ~ water ~ learned from boilers_charm
~ "Calls water out of rock, or out of a flooded way. Here. Power 2."
~ then set flask.water: brine when flask.water == empty
~ then lower stair_water 2 when here in [brine_pans, sump]
act sweeten: cost 2 ~ spell ~ water ~ learned from boilers_charm
~ "Takes the salt out of water. Range: touch."
~ when flask.water == brine
~ then set flask.water: fresh
act clear: cost 4 ~ spell ~ learned from chalk_charm
~ "Shifts a fall of stone. Range: touch. Power 2: two loads."
~ when here == marrow and rubble > 0
~ then lower rubble 2
act dowse: cost 1 ~ spell ~ air ~ learned from dowsing
~ "Tells you which way the air goes out. Range: the mine."

combo freshet: draw, sweeten ~ spell ~ water ~ learned from notes_greater
~ "Fresh water, all at once, at one thing. Range: here. Power 1: one ward of salt."
~ at npc here where: it.salted
~ then lower target.salt 1
combo firebrand: kindle, gust ~ spell ~ fire ~ learned from notes_greater
~ "A flame thrown into the next place. Range: next."
~ at place where: it.next_to(here) and it.timbered and it.heat == 0 and not it.burnt
~ then set target.heat: 1
combo shroud: glimmer, hush ~ spell ~ quiet ~ learned from notes_greater
~ "No warmth, no sound, from you or what you carry. Self. Lasts 4 turns."
~ then set me.shrouded: yes ~ for 4 turns
combo bridge: knit, shore ~ spell ~ learned from notes_greater
~ "A fallen shaft stands once more, for one crossing. Range: next."
~ at place where: it.next_to(here) and it.like(shaft) and it.fallen
~ then set target.fallen: no
~ then set target.crossings: 1
combo updraught: gust, lighten ~ spell ~ air ~ learned from notes_greater
~ "You ride the air up the cage shaft, with no cage. Self."
~ when here == incline

(((
The book's Links, offered wherever you are, outside a fight: one per
spell, and one per target where a spell has a range. Each goes to a short
passage saying what happened. A spell you have not learned is not offered.
)))
> ~ for apprentice ~ everywhere
> [[Kindle {target}->spell:kindle]] ~ kindle
> [[Glimmer->spell:glimmer]] ~ glimmer
> [[Quench->spell:quench]] ~ quench
> [[Gust into {target}->spell:gust]] ~ gust
> [[Hush->spell:hush]] ~ hush
> [[Ward->spell:ward]] ~ ward
> [[Tongue->spell:tongue]] ~ tongue
> [[Knit {target}->spell:knit]] ~ knit
> [[Shore->spell:shore]] ~ shore
> [[Lighten {target}->spell:lighten]] ~ lighten
> [[Draw->spell:draw]] ~ draw
> [[Sweeten->spell:sweeten]] ~ sweeten
> [[Clear->spell:clear]] ~ clear
> [[Dowse->dowse]] ~ dowse
> [[Freshet at {target}->warden:freshet]] ~ freshet
> [[Firebrand into {target}->spell:firebrand]] ~ firebrand
> [[Shroud->spell:shroud]] ~ shroud
> [[Bridge {target}->spell:bridge]] ~ bridge
> [[Updraught->pithead]] ~ updraught

:: thwaite [npc]
state found: no
state with_me: no
state lightened: no
--

:: warden [npc]
state salt: 3
state roused: no
state paid: no
state unmade: no
--
(((
Down is free; up is paid. The Warden rouses when someone leaves the
Marrow with marrow salt (`warden:wakes`). Roused, it
follows one place every two turns, on salt only, and never into fire;
when it reaches you, it fights.
)))
pattern blows: crush, grasp, crush, douse ~ repeat ~ one per round

threat crush: at me ~ answered by cover
~ then wound target 1
threat grasp: at me ~ answered by cover
~ then set me.held: yes ~ for 1 turn
threat douse: at me ~ answered by cover
~ then set lamp.lit: no
~ then set safety_lamp.lit: no

:: gleaner [npc]
state candle_lit: yes
state met: no
--
(((
The Gleaner wanders the upper workings with a candle. In a place you are
not in, they take one loose thing worth having. In a dry timbered place,
their candle may start a fire. Gust blows it out; they light it again
three turns later.
)))
on turn ends when not gleaner.here
~ then give one(item, in: gleaner.place, where: it.like(treasure) or it.like(tool)) to gleaner
~ then roll candle when gleaner.candle_lit and gleaner.place.timbered and not gleaner.place.burnt and gleaner.place.heat == 0
~ then set gleaner.candle_lit: yes ~ after 3 turns when not gleaner.candle_lit

table candle: roll d6
~ 1: then set gleaner.place.heat: 1
~ 2..=6: nothing

:: prologue [prologue]
learn primer
--
Saltmarrow is a town of eleven chimneys on the edge of a fen, and under it is a mine that grows salt the way a cellar grows mushrooms: slowly, in the dark, and worth a great deal more than it looks.

The salt here holds a spell. Put a crystal on your tongue and say the word, and the salt is spent and the word is done. That is the whole of the trade, and Agnes Thwaite is the last saltwright in the town who knows it, and three days ago she went down for marrow salt before the winter and did not come back up.

The pumps have stopped. Nobody else will go. You are her apprentice, and you have her lamp, her primer, a flask, and four crystals in a twist of paper.

> [[Go to the pithead->pithead]]

:: pithead
--
[if not seeing]
Night. The headframe is a black shape against a blacker sky.

[else]
The winding house of Saltmarrow pit: a tall timber headframe over the cage shaft, a cold engine, a coat on a peg that you know is Thwaite’s. A hatch in the floor opens on the ladderway. Beyond the door, the fen goes on for ever in the fog.

[if not cage_fixed]
The cage is somewhere at the bottom of its shaft. Its rope hangs slack. You could climb down it. You could not climb up.

[if thwaite.here]
Thwaite sits down on the step of the winding house and laughs, once, like a cough.

[end]
> [[Put {target} in the salt chest->pithead:chest]] ~ at item where: it.held_by(me) and it.like(treasure) and not it.counted
> [[Go home with her->home]] ~ when thwaite.here
> [[Go home without her->alone]] ~ when not thwaite.here

:: pithead:chest [act]
move target to chest
set target.counted: yes
raise score 10
--
You lay {target} in the salt chest, where the next saltwright will find it.

:: ladderway
--
[if not seeing]
Rungs, cold under your hands, going down into nothing. You stop. You do not go down a ladder you cannot see.

[else]
A ladder of salt-bleached pine, bolted down a square shaft. Landings every twenty feet. You are {plural(here.depth, "foot")} down and halfway.

[if here.burnt]
The rungs are charcoal. They hold. You would not say they hold well.

[if here.heat == 1]
Smoke curls up between the rungs from somewhere below.

[end]

:: shaft:creaks
(((
The warnings, one for each crossing left. The mice go first.
)))
--
[if entered.crossings > 2]
The shored timber creaks, and holds. The mice watch with interest.

[if entered.crossings == 2]
The burnt timber groans under you. {capital(plural(entered.crossings, "mouse"))} watch you from a crack, and do not like what they see.

[if entered.crossings == 1]
A rung snaps and drops away into the dark, and you hear it land a long time later. One mouse is left in the crack. It is packing.

[if entered.crossings == 0]
No mice. The whole shaft sways like a ship. This is the last time anyone crosses it.

:: shaft:falls
--
Behind you, with a long tired sigh, {left} falls in.

:: gallery
hint: "The air in the deep is bad because nothing moves it."
--
[if not seeing]
A great dark place. Your voice goes a long way and does not come back.

[else]
The Long Gallery: a hall cut out of grey salt, its roof held up by pillars the first salters left standing, each as thick as a cottage. Rail tracks run west into the stables and down the Incline. To the east, an arch into a chapel. North, the timber yard.

A canvas air door hangs across the Incline’s mouth{if air_door_open then ", tied back" else ", propped shut with a shovel"}.

Thwaite’s satchel lies against a pillar, as if she put it down to have both hands free.

[if here.veins > 0 and me.holds.pick]
The pillars glitter. There is good salt here, for anyone with a pick.

[end]
> [[Open Thwaite’s satchel->gallery:satchel]] ~ once
> [[Tie back the air door->gallery:air_door]] ~ when not air_door_open
> [[Prise a crystal from a pillar->prise]] ~ uses pick ~ when here.veins > 0 and me.holds.pick and not pick.broken

:: gallery:satchel [act]
learn notes_mending
learn notes_weight
learn notes_greater
gain salt 2
--
A spare pair of socks, two crystals in a twist of paper, and her notebook, open at the page she was reading: knit, shore, lighten, and a list of five greater workings, two words said as one.

:: gallery:air_door [act]
set air_door_open: yes
--
You pull the shovel and tie the canvas back. At once there is a draught on your neck, going north, into the drift: the mine breathing again, after three days holding its breath.

:: prise [act]
lower here.veins 1
gain salt 1
--
[if pick.broken]
The head of the pick flies off and rings away across the floor. You keep the crystal.

[else]
Three blows, and a crystal the size of a thumbnail drops into your palm.

:: chapel
hint: "Salters carved their workings where they prayed."
--
[if not seeing]
Your lamp is out, and somewhere close is a smell of candle wax and old stone.

[else]
The salters carved a chapel out of the salt itself: altar, pews, a pulpit with steps, all one piece, and a chandelier of salt that throws your lamplight back at you a thousandfold. On the walls, in a hand nobody has written for two hundred years, workings.

[if salt_rose.in(chapel)]
On the altar, a rose carved out of pink salt.

[end]
> [[Read the carvings->chapel:carvings]] ~ once

:: chapel:carvings [act]
learn carving_hush
learn carving_ward
learn carving_tongue
learn warden_feels
raise score 5
--
Three workings, carved for miners who needed them: one to walk unheard, one to turn a blow, one *to speak with the Warden, which was made, and not born*. Under the last, smaller: *It feels warmth and hears feet. It has no eyes, and wants none.*

:: stables
hint: "A coat on a nail has pockets."
--
[if not seeing]
Straw underfoot, and the smell of horse, though there has not been a horse here for fifty years.

[else]
Pit-pony stables, timber stalls in a row, each with a name painted over it: SAMSON, DUCHESS, LITTLE JOHN, PEG. The hay in the racks is fifty years dry. A coat hangs on a nail in Peg’s stall.

[if brasses.in(stables)]
A strap of pony brasses hangs over Samson’s door.

[if horseshoe.in(stables)]
A horseshoe is nailed over the door, ends up, for luck.

[if here.heat == 1]
The hay is smouldering. It smells, for a moment, almost nice.

[if gleaner.here]
The Gleaner is going through the hay with a candle, very carefully, as if they had heard about hay and candles.

[end]
> [[Search the coat->stables:coat]] ~ once ~ then set stables.searched: yes
> [[Fill the lamp from the oil can->stables:oil]] ~ once ~ when me.holds.lamp or me.holds.safety_lamp

:: stables:coat [act]
gain tally
--
A pipe, no tobacco, and a brass pay tally stamped **41**. Somebody’s day’s wage, never collected.

:: stables:oil [act]
raise lamp_oil 60
--
You fill the lamp to the brim. It will burn a long while yet.

:: timber_yard
--
[if not seeing]
You walk into a stack of something wooden. It does not fall on you, this time.

[else]
The timber yard, where the props were kept: staves stacked to the roof, a saw-horse, a rack of tools, a board where the deputy chalked the day’s orders. The last order is a working.

[end]
> [[Read the chalk board->timber_yard:board]] ~ once

:: timber_yard:board [act]
learn chalk_charm
--
CLEAR, it says, and under it, in a different hand: *a load at a time, and prop as you go, you fool.*

:: incline
--
[if not seeing]
The floor slopes. Something on rails creaks somewhere below.

[else]
The Incline: a haulage road sloping down into the second level, rails and a line of tubs, props every yard holding up a roof that clearly wants to come down. At the foot of the slope is the cage, in its shaft, with a hand winch bolted inside it for the deputies: a jack roll, for winding the cage up its own rope.

East to the brine pans. West, the north drift, and a smell like a struck match.

[if not cage_fixed]
The jack roll’s pawl is missing. Without it the winch will not hold, and nobody is going up that way.

[if cage_fixed]
The new pawl clicks over the ratchet. The jack roll will hold.

[end]
> [[Fit the pawl to the jack roll->incline:pawl]] ~ when me.holds.pawl and not cage_fixed

:: incline:pawl [act]
set cage_fixed: yes
lose pawl
raise score 5
--
The pawl drops onto the ratchet with a click you feel in your teeth. Somebody could wind themselves up this shaft now, if they had the arms for it.

:: drift
(((
Firedamp. An open flame here caps blue the first turn, a warning, and
fires the second. Gust or the air door clears it.
)))
--
[if gas > 0 and open_flame]
Your lamp flame stands up tall and turns blue. It has never done that before.

[if not seeing]
A narrow place, and a smell like a struck match. Somewhere ahead, the air hisses.

[if seeing and (gas == 0 or not open_flame)]
The north drift: a narrow working that goes on north toward a square of timber cribs, the top of the winze. A deputy’s kit lies by the wall, as if dropped in a hurry.

[end]
> [[Put the lamp out->drift:lamp_out]] ~ when lamp.lit and me.holds.lamp
> [[Open the deputy’s kit->drift:kit]] ~ once ~ when seeing and (gas == 0 or not open_flame) ~ then set drift.searched: yes

:: drift:lamp_out [act]
set lamp.lit: no
learn blue_cap
--
You pinch the wick. Dark. Somewhere ahead of you, the air hisses gently, like a kettle thinking about it.

:: drift:kit [act]
--
Chalk, a notebook of gas readings that stop three days ago, and a cylinder of fine iron gauze, the kind that goes round a lamp flame so the flame cannot get out.

:: drift:fires
set gas: 0
set cribbing.heat: 1 when not cribbing.burnt
wound me 1
--
The gas goes up with a soft enormous WHUMPH, and the whole drift is light for a moment, and then you are on your back with your eyebrows gone and the cribs at the end of the drift are on fire.

:: cribbing
--
[if not seeing]
A square hole, a ladder down it, and the dark.

[else]
The cribbed winze: a square shaft down to the deep, lined with timber cribs laid like a log cabin turned on its end. A ladder down the middle. Cold air comes up it, and a sound like a very large thing breathing slowly.

[if here.burnt]
The cribs are burnt black, and creak, and drop flakes of charcoal like snow.

[end]

:: brine_pans
--
[if not seeing]
Water laps somewhere at your feet. It smells of the sea.

[else]
Brine pans: wide iron trays where brine was boiled down to salt, their fires long cold. The brine has dried in them to a white crust. Under one pan rim, a charm is scratched. To the south a stair goes down{if stair_water > 0 then " into black water, {plural(stair_water, "step")} deep" else ", wet and dripping, to the sump"}.

[if here.crust > 0]
Fresh crust has formed on the near pan, about {plural(here.crust, "crystal")} of it.

[end]
> [[Scrape up the crust->scrape]] ~ when here.crust > 0
> [[Read the charm under the rim->brine_pans:charm]] ~ once
> [[Fill your flask with brine->brine_pans:fill]] ~ when flask.water == empty
> [[Open the drain cock with the spanner->brine_pans:drain]] ~ when me.holds.spanner and stair_water > 0

:: scrape [act]
gain salt here.crust
set here.crust: 0
--
You scrape the crust up with your thumbnail and come away with salt. Slowly, it begins again.

:: brine_pans:charm [act]
learn boilers_charm
--
Two workings, for the boilers: *draw*, to call water out of rock, and *sweeten*, to take the salt out of it. Somebody has added, in pencil: *useful for tea*.

:: brine_pans:fill [act]
set flask.water: brine
--
You fill the flask. It is salt enough to float an egg.

:: brine_pans:drain [act]
set stair_water: 0
raise score 5
--
The cock is stiff, then not, and somewhere under your feet a great deal of water goes gurgling away down an old drain. The stair to the south comes up out of the water step by step.

:: sump
--
[if not seeing]
Running water, loud, close.

[else]
The sump, where the mine’s water gathers. A spring has broken in through the east wall and pours down in a sheet: not brine, but *fresh* water, sweet as rain. That is what is flooding Saltmarrow. That is what is eating the salt. A sluice wheel stands beside a channel that runs north into the Warden’s hall.

[end]
> [[Fill your flask at the spring->sump:fill]] ~ when flask.water != fresh
> [[Turn the sluice wheel->sump:sluice]] ~ when me.holds.spanner and not sluice_open

:: sump:fill [act]
set flask.water: fresh
--
You hold the flask under the spring until it is full and your hand aches with the cold.

:: sump:sluice [act]
set sluice_open: yes
--
The wheel turns. Fresh water runs north along the channel, into the Warden’s hall, over its salt floor.

:: wardens_hall
--
[if not seeing]
A vast dark. Something in it, very large, that does not breathe at all.

[else]
The Warden’s hall: salt columns going up into the dark, a door west to the sump, an arch north into the Marrow.

[if warden.here and not warden.unmade]
Between the columns, standing as it has stood for two hundred years, the Brinewarden. It is twice your height, a figure of grey salt bound with black pit timber and iron bands, and where a face should be it has a miner’s lamp{if warden.paid then ", lit" else ", unlit"}.

[if not warden.here and not warden.unmade]
The place between the columns where the Warden stood is empty. Its footprints go away across the salt.

[if sluice_open and warden.here and not warden.unmade]
Fresh water runs over the floor around its feet. The salt of its feet is beginning, very slowly, to go soft.

[if warden.unmade]
A heap of grey salt and old timber, and iron bands, and a lamp lying on its side.

[if warden.paid and warden.here]
It stands aside.

[if me.tongued and warden.here and not warden.paid and not warden.unmade]
@warden Down is free. Up is paid.

[end]
> ~ when warden.here and not warden.unmade
> [[Fight->warden:fight]] ~ when warden.roused
> [[Ask the Warden what it is owed->wardens_hall:ask]] ~ when me.tongued and not warden.paid
> [[Pay the Warden with the tally->wardens_hall:pay]] ~ when me.tongued and me.holds.tally and not warden.paid
> [[Give the Warden back the shard->wardens_hall:return]] ~ when me.tongued and me.holds.shard and not warden.paid

:: wardens_hall:ask [act]
learn never_paid
--
@warden I was made to keep the deep. For a wage. Forty were paid on the first Friday. Forty-one was me. Forty-one was not paid.

:: wardens_hall:pay [act]
give tally to warden
set warden.paid: yes
set warden.roused: no
raise score 10
--
You hold out the brass tally. The Warden takes it between two fingers of salt, and turns it over, and reads the number. Then the lamp in its face catches, and burns, small and steady, and it steps aside.

@warden Paid. I will carry her, if she will be carried, as far as the salt goes.

:: wardens_hall:return [act]
give shard to warden
set warden.roused: no
--
You give back the shard. The Warden fits it into its own chest, where there is a hole exactly that shape, and stands still again.

@warden Up is paid.

:: marrow
--
[if not seeing]
Light from nowhere: the walls themselves are faintly bright, the way snow is at night.

[else]
The Marrow: a cave of salt so pure it is clear, so that the walls go down into themselves like ice on a deep pond, and the light of your lamp goes into them and does not come back. At the far end a fall of rock blocks a low tunnel.

[if not thwaite.found]
And sitting against the fall with her leg out in front of her at an angle legs should not have: Agnes Thwaite, with a shard of marrow salt beside her, the size of a loaf.

[if thwaite.found and thwaite.here and not thwaite.with_me]
Thwaite, against the fall, waiting.

[if rubble > 0 and propped]
Staves are set under the roof of the fall.

[if here.crust > 0]
Where the walls meet the floor, new salt has grown, like frost on a step.

[end]
> [[Thwaite!->marrow:found]] ~ when not thwaite.found
> [[Take her with you->marrow:take_her]] ~ when thwaite.found and thwaite.here and not thwaite.with_me and way_free
> [[Set staves under the fall->marrow:prop]] ~ when rubble > 0 and not propped and count(stave, held by: me) >= 2
> [[Gather the new salt->scrape]] ~ when here.crust > 0
> [[Dig at the fall->marrow:dig]] ~ uses pick ~ when rubble > 0 and propped and me.holds.pick and not pick.broken

:: marrow:found [act]
set thwaite.found: yes
learn never_paid
learn dowsing
learn boilers_charm
gain salt 3
raise score 10
--
@thwaite Took you long enough.

She has been here three days. She cut the shard, and the Warden would not let her by with it, and she would not leave it, and she tried the old adit instead, and the adit came down on her leg.

@thwaite Down is free, it says. Up is paid. It means the salt. Leave the shard and it’ll let us by, and I’ll never forgive either of us. (she presses three crystals into your hand) And here. Dowse. Tastes of the way out.

@thwaite And if the winze is down, the stair by the sump drains with *draw*, two steps a go. Salt grows back in here, slowly. You won’t starve of it.

@thwaite One more thing. It was made to guard this place for a wage, and nobody ever paid it. Don’t fight it if you can help it. It’s only doing what it was made for.

:: thwaite:waiting
--
Thwaite is here, sitting on the floor where your working ran out, with her leg out in front of her.

@thwaite Well? I’m not walking.

> [[Lighten {target}->spell:lighten]] ~ lighten
> [[Roll her onto the stretcher->marrow:take_her]] ~ when me.holds.stretcher

:: marrow:take_her [act]
set thwaite.with_me: yes
--
[if warden.paid]
The Warden comes in, stooping under the arch, and lifts her as if she were a coat.

[if not warden.paid and me.holds.stretcher]
You roll her onto the stretcher. She says a word the primer does not have.

[if not warden.paid and not me.holds.stretcher]
She rises off the floor like a leaf on a draught, and says, crossly, that she could get used to this.

:: marrow:prop [act]
set propped: yes
lose stave 2
--
You set two staves under the roof of the fall, and wedge them tight. The roof stops whispering.

:: marrow:dig [act]
lower rubble 1
--
You dig, and haul, and dig. A load of rock comes away.

[if rubble == 0]
Cold air on your face, and the smell of the fen. The adit is open.

:: warden:wakes
(((
Out by the hall, with marrow salt. Whether the Warden feels you is
decided here: shrouded, or hushed with no flame, it does not. Roused,
it is slow, and you have a head start: walk on, and it follows.
)))
let unfelt: me.shrouded or (me.hushed and not open_flame)
set warden.roused: yes when not warden.paid and not warden.unmade and not unfelt
--
[if warden.roused]
The lamp in the Warden’s face does not light. But it turns its head toward you all the same, slowly, with a sound like a millstone, and takes one step.

[if not warden.roused and not warden.paid and not warden.unmade]
You go past it close enough to touch. It does not turn its head.

:: adit
--
[if not seeing]
A low wet tunnel. You walk bent double, with water round your ankles.

[else]
The old adit: a drainage tunnel the first salters drove out to the fen, low and wet and very long. At the end, daylight, cut into strips by the stop-planks across its mouth.

[end]
> [[Knock out the stop-planks->adit:planks]] ~ when not planks_out and me.holds.hammer
> [[Hold the lamp to the stop-planks->adit:burn]] ~ when not planks_out and me.holds.lamp and lamp.lit

:: adit:planks [act]
set planks_out: yes
set stair_water: 0
raise score 5
--
Three blows each. The planks go, and the water of the whole mine goes with them, past your knees and out into the fen in a brown roar, and when it is done there is daylight.

:: adit:burn [act]
set planks_out: yes ~ after 2 turns
set stair_water: 0 ~ after 2 turns
raise score 5
--
The planks are tarred, and take the flame at once. In two turns there will be nothing but a black frame and daylight. Until then, a great deal of smoke.

:: fen
--
Reeds, fog, a heron that looks at you with deep disapproval. Saltmarrow’s eleven chimneys, a mile off. The adit mouth behind you pours water into the fen.

> [[Go home with her->home]] ~ when thwaite.here
> [[Go home without her->alone]] ~ when not thwaite.here

:: fire:turn
(((
Each turn's fire, in order. A blaze burns out. A smoulder or a fire grows.
Each blaze, before it burns out, reaches the nearest timbered place next
to it that has not burnt and is not burning. The brine pans and
the Marrow crust over again too, one crystal every four turns, up to
three. If Thwaite has been left where fire reaches, she drags herself out
to the nearest place that is not timber.
)))
let ablaze: all(place, where: it.heat == 3)
let growing: all(place, where: it.heat in 1..=2)
let blows: here == drift and gas > 0 and open_flame and flame_warned
spreads 1 from ablaze to nearest(place, where: it.timbered and it.heat == 0 and not it.burnt) ~ along way ~ within 1 ~ then set it.heat: 1
destroy all(item, in: ablaze, where: it.burns)
set ablaze.heat: 0
set ablaze.burnt: yes
raise growing.heat 1
let crusting: all(place, where: it.crusts and it.crust < 3)
raise crusting.crust 1 when clock.now % 4 == 0
lower gas 1 when air_door_open and gas > 0
move thwaite to nearest(place, where: it.heat == 0 and not it.timbered) ~ along way when thwaite.place.heat > 0 and not thwaite.here
set flame_warned: yes when here == drift and gas > 0 and open_flame
set flame_warned: no when here != drift
--
[if count(burning_near) > 0]
Smoke drifts in from {list burning_near}.

[if here.heat == 1]
The timbers here are smouldering.

[if here.heat == 2]
The timbers around you are burning. Get out.

[if blows; then play drift:fires]
[if here.heat == 3; then play burned]

:: dowse [act]
let out: nearest(place, where: it.way_out) ~ along way
let step: here.toward(out)
--
The salt on your tongue tastes, faintly, of {out}. The air goes that way: by {step}.

:: spell:kindle [act]
(((
What each spell does is in the book (its act). These passages say what
it looked like, and do what only one place needs: hay, and the planks.
)))
set stables.heat: 1 when target == hay and not stables.burnt
set planks_out: yes ~ after 2 turns when target == stop_planks
set stair_water: 0 ~ after 2 turns when target == stop_planks
raise score 5 when target == stop_planks
--
Salt on the tongue, then the word, and a flame stands up on your fingertip like a small polite guest.

[if target == hay]
The hay takes it at once, gratefully, and then all of it at once, ungratefully.

[if target == stop_planks]
The tar on the planks catches. Smoke rolls down the adit toward you, and daylight starts to show through the cracks.

:: spell:glimmer [act]
--
A light comes up around you like the light off snow. It gives no heat at all. Your breath still shows in it.

:: spell:quench [act]
--
You say the word at the fire, and the fire sits down.

[if here.heat > 0]
It is not out. It is thinking about it.

:: spell:gust [act]
--
You breathe out, and the breath keeps going, out of your mouth and down the way into {target}.

[if target == drift]
The bad air goes with it, north and up and out.

:: spell:hush [act]
--
The sound of your own feet goes away. It is like walking in a dream of walking.

:: spell:ward [act]
--
A skin of salt grows over you, thin as frost on a window.

:: spell:tongue [act]
--
Your tongue goes numb, then strange, then fluent in a language nobody born has ever spoken.

:: spell:knit [act]
--
{capital(target)} mends with a click, like a bone set by someone who knows how.

:: spell:shore [act]
--
The burnt timber creaks, and stops creaking. It will hold three crossings more. The mice, cautiously, come back.

:: spell:lighten [act]
--
{capital(target)} stops weighing anything at all, and looks surprised about it.

:: spell:draw [act]
--
[if here in [brine_pans, sump] and stair_water > 0]
The water in the stair draws back two steps, sulking, into the rock.

[if here in [brine_pans, sump] and stair_water == 0]
The last of the water in the stair drains away into the rock.

[else]
Water beads out of the bare rock and runs into your flask, salt as tears.

:: spell:sweeten [act]
--
The salt in the flask settles to the bottom like snow, and the water over it is sweet.

:: spell:clear [act]
--
Two loads of rock lift off the fall and stack themselves against the wall, very neatly, as if ashamed.

[if rubble == 0]
Cold air on your face, and the smell of the fen. The adit is open.

:: spell:firebrand [act]
--
Kindle and gust, said as one: a flame leaves your hand and goes down the way into {target}, and finds the timber there.

:: spell:shroud [act]
--
Glimmer and hush, said as one. Cold light, no sound. You could be a ghost. You could be nothing.

:: spell:bridge [act]
--
Knit and shore, said as one. The broken timber of {target} draws itself together out of the dark and stands, for now, long enough for one crossing.

:: warden:fight [encounter]
encounter warden
~ round by round
~ acts last
~ until warden.salt == 0 or me.down
--
The Warden comes for you, slowly, the way a tide comes in. It has three wards of salt, and fresh water undoes salt.

> [[Begin->warden:round]]

:: warden:round [round]
let next: warden.blows.next
--
[if next == crush]
It draws back an arm like a bucket on a rope.

[if next == grasp]
It opens its hand, wide, at the height of your waist.

[if next == douse]
Its chest swells. Something in it sloshes.

[if sluice_open and warden.in(wardens_hall)]
The fresh water round its feet eats at it. A little more of it is gone each round.

[end]
> ~ for apprentice
> [[Freshet at {target}->warden:freshet]] ~ freshet
> [[Throw the flask of spring water->warden:flask]] ~ when flask.water == fresh
> [[Ward->warden:ward]] ~ ward
> [[Kindle its bindings->warden:bindings]] ~ cost 1
> [[Let it come->warden:blow]] ~ pass
> [[Run for it->here]] ~ when not me.held ~ then end encounter

:: warden:freshet [act]
--
Draw and sweeten, said as one: a gout of sweet water out of the bare rock, straight at its chest. Where it hits, the salt runs like sugar in tea.

:: warden:flask [act]
lower warden.salt 1
set flask.water: empty
--
You throw the spring water. It goes into the salt with a hiss, and a hole opens in the Warden’s side.

:: warden:ward [act]
--
A skin of salt over you, thin as frost.

:: warden:bindings [act]
lower warden.salt 1
--
Kindle, at the black timber that binds it. The old pitch catches. The Warden stamps it out, but one band of iron falls ringing to the floor.

:: warden:blow [resolve]
lower warden.salt 1 when sluice_open and warden.in(wardens_hall)
set warden.unmade: yes when warden.salt == 0
set warden.roused: no when warden.salt == 0
--
[if threat.name == crush and threat.outcome == hit]
A fist of salt the size of a bucket. You are on the floor, and do not remember getting there.

[if threat.name == grasp and threat.outcome == hit]
It takes you round the middle. You cannot run.

[if threat.name == douse and threat.outcome == hit]
It breathes brine at you, and your lamp goes out.

[if threat.outcome == cover]
The blow lands on your ward, and the ward cracks like ice, and you are still standing.

[if warden.unmade]
It comes apart: grey salt, black timber, iron bands ringing on the floor, a lamp rolling away on its side. It was only doing what it was made for.

[end]
> [[Next round->warden:round]] ~ when not warden.unmade and me.up
> [[Step over what is left of it->here]] ~ when warden.unmade

:: gleaner:about
let first: not gleaner.met
set gleaner.met: yes
--
[if first]
Someone is here before you: a small person in three coats, with a candle in a jam jar and a sack over one shoulder. The sack clinks.

@gleaner Finders keepers. Losers can buy it back. Two crystals a thing. I’m not greedy.

[else]
The Gleaner is here{if gleaner.candle_lit then ", candle in hand" else ", in the dark, sulking"}.

[end]
> [[Buy back {target}->gleaner:buy]] ~ at item where: it.held_by(gleaner) ~ cost 2
> [[Ask the Gleaner about the deep->gleaner:deep]] ~ once

:: gleaner:buy [act]
give target to me
--
Two crystals change hands, and {target} comes out of the sack, a little dustier.

:: gleaner:deep [act]
learn blue_cap
learn warden_feels
--
@gleaner Never take a bare flame up the north drift. If it goes tall and blue, run. (they think) And the big thing at the bottom. It doesn’t see. It feels you warm, and it hears you walk. I go past it cold and in my socks.

:: crushed [ending]
--
[if here == drift]
The drift lights up, all of it, and so, briefly, do you.

[else]
The salt comes down on you like a wave on a beach, and the beach is you.

[end]

> [[Undo->here]] ~ rewind

:: burned [ending]
--
You walk into the heat, or the heat walks into you. There is a great deal of light and then none.

> [[Undo->here]] ~ rewind

:: home [finale]
raise score 20
raise score 10 when not warden.unmade
--
You come up into the grey morning with Agnes Thwaite, and the shard, or not, and nobody in Saltmarrow will ever quite believe what you tell them about the Warden.

[if warden.paid]
Somewhere under your feet, a lamp is burning that has not burned for two hundred years. It was paid.

[end]
Your score is {score} of 100, which makes you {rank}.

:: alone [finale]
--
You go home. The fen fog comes in behind you. Somewhere under your feet, Thwaite is waiting, and in the morning you will have to decide whether to go back down.

Your score is {score} of 100, which makes you {rank}.

:: a_burnt_ladder_holds_three_crossings [test]
start: ladderway
given: set ladderway.burnt: yes
expect: ladderway.crossings == 3

:: the_warden_lets_you_in [test]
start: wardens_hall
expect: not warden.roused

:: a_paid_warden_carries_her [test]
start: marrow
given: set thwaite.found: yes
given: set warden.paid: yes
do: "Take her with you"
expect: thwaite.with_me
expect: not warden.roused

:: firedamp_warns_first [test]
start: drift
given: set gas: 3
expect: not flame_warned
expect link: "Put the lamp out"
